# Graphify artifacts (tracked — see .gitignore).
#
# graph.json and graph.html are regenerated wholesale on every AST refresh, so a
# line diff is 140k lines of noise that also makes `git status` and `git diff`
# slow. Marking them -diff keeps git from attempting a textual diff at all.
#
# `merge=graphify` completes the union merge driver that `git config` already
# registers (merge.graphify.driver). Without this line git never invokes it and
# a two-branch refresh produces an unresolvable conflict in the JSON.
graphify-out/graph.json -diff merge=graphify
graphify-out/graph.html -diff

# The knowledgebase is deliberately NOT marked -diff: memory/, reflections/ and
# findings/decisions.jsonl are the durable record, and reviewing how a verdict
# changed is the whole point of tracking them.
